k\\":\\"2025-06-02\\",\\"grade\\":\\"F\\"}]"', '"[]"', '"[{\\"start_date\\":\\"2024-04-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"Present\\",\\"company\\":\\"NIRIIS SHIPPING SA\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"NIRIIS SHIPPING SA\\",\\"company_id\\":35677880,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/niriis-shipping-sa\\",\\"department\\":\\"Engineering\\",\\"title\\":\\"Technical Superintendent\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"senior\\",\\"description\\":\\"Oversee the daily operations of vessels\' maintenance and repair, budgeting, survey schedules, onboard general assessment of vessels, inspections and docking, etc. Ensure that the assigned vessels are technically operational or otherwise managed accordingly to the management agreement requirement. Attend to vessels\' dry docking, repairs and survey when required and determine repair specifications for dry docking and maintenance. Provide and compile documented reports upon completion of dry docking, including summaries of works performed, operational budgets, and actual expenditures. Identify and source for technical and operational supplies required for the vessels and ensure the rates are most economical. Provide technical assistance and advice to ships both at home port and overseas. Perform monthly review of logs processes and attend to vessel inspections. Monitor technical status of vessel with relation to class cert and survey. Perform technical compliance audits and investigation on defects\\\\/failures on a regular scheduled basis to ensure conformance. Work closely with the HSE Management team to ensure smooth and successful implementation of QHSE system and policies for the Division. Undertake any other Technical related assignments as and when required. Plan and supervise all organizational and technical activities, regarding PMS technical issues. Liaise with other departments within the company to ensure the smooth operation and implementation of the Company\\\\u2019s PMS System. Monitor the PMS system operation (vessels performance, corrections, additions, communication with vessels and relevant IT departments). Ensure that data entries both digital and hard copies (BENEFIT, EvByte, Tech folders, drawings and manuals) are maintained properly. BENEFIT software structural and operational expert. Assistant to the Technical Manager, cooperation with the Fleet Managers.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"Systems\\",\\"is_current\\":true},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2024-02-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2024-04-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"EDIT AUTOMATION LTD.\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"EDIT AUTOMATION LTD.\\",\\"company_id\\":2176208,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/edit-automation\\",\\"department\\":\\"Operations\\",\\"title\\":\\"Operations Manager\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"manager\\",\\"description\\":\\"Responsible to approve budgets and legal bounds, manage the Company safely, profitably and in a way to preserve Company assets. To be kept informed of market developments, with a view to expand Company\\\\u2019s activities in areas of interest and to follow-up special opportunities, subject to board approval and without exceeding approved budgets. Responsible for monitoring, revision and conclusion of contracts. Responsible for finance and insurance. To interface with Authorities and Corporate Bodies. Responsible for strategic planning and budgeting for the Company. To assign authority and responsibilities and maintain a competent workforce. To monitor performance through the internal audits. Responsible for Office Personnel management. Responsible to supervise progress of works based on the relevant budgets. Liaise closely with the company\'s CEO and provide all necessary quidelines. To appraise all office personnel and verify periodically whether all those undertaking tasks are acting in conformity with the Company\\\\u2019s responsibilities code.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"Logistics\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2022-04-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2024-02-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Niriis Shipping S.A.\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Niriis Shipping S.A.\\",\\"company_id\\":35677880,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/niriis-shipping-sa\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Engineering Superintendent - PMS Coordinator\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Plan and supervise all organizational and technical activities, regarding PMS technical issues and Company\\\\u2019s fleet maintenance schedules. Monitor, control and perform required actions to ensure the quality of the repairs and projects carried out by the Department. Liaise with other departments within the company to ensure the smooth operation and implementation of the Company\\\\u2019s PMS System. Liaise with other companies\\\\u2019 departments. Monitor the PMS system operation (vessels performance, corrections, additions, communication with vessels and relevant IT departments). Ensure that data entries both digital and hard copies (BENEFIT, EvByte, Tech folders, drawings and manuals) are maintained properly. Assist the proper management of spare parts, engine stores. Technical Superintendent duties, assistant to the Technical Manager, cooperation with the Fleet Managers.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2016-09-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2021-12-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"FNT at SEA SERVICES Ltd\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"FNT at SEA SERVICES Ltd\\",\\"company_id\\":29319476,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/fnt-advanced-services\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Maritime Surveyor\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Conduct condition monitoring and technical surveying on various types of machinery equipment on vessels to identify significant changes in machines that includes testing like hull vibration, machinery vibrations, infrared thermography, ultrasonic research, motor current signature analysis, and sound level surveys. Report results to identify faults in machinery and support operational decisions on equipment\\\\u2019s condition. Liaise with crew members and company superintendents to complete tasks while providing technical advice, support, and training.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2014-10-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2016-08-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"HELLENIC NAVY\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"HELLENIC NAVY\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Staff Officer, ILS and Offsets Division\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Supported fleet research department with Industrial Logistic Systems (ILS) and Offsets benefit operations, including ERP application, aviation equipment marketplace, and marine defence. Oversaw fleet performance and statistics to identify and manage risks. Acted as material inventory officer, ensuring sufficient stock of materials and reporting insufficient or depleted inventory. Translated research and technical documentation for company from Greek to English and vice versa.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2013-01-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2014-10-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy GS\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy GS\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"Human_resources\\",\\"title\\":\\"Staff Officer, Human Resources, Hellenic Navy GS\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Completed operational, administrative, and logistical functions for unit that involved updating personal information and transfer requirements for approximately 2.5K officers using MS Office applications. Performed staff evaluations and career counselling for officers while serving as personnel point system master operator. Drafted outgoing reports\\\\/correspondence and liaised with officials from federal organisations to address staff issues. Reviewed accuracy of hardcopy files for each officer to transfer data to official online system.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2011-09-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2013-01-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Chief Engineer, HS DOIRANI\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Filled various roles as chief engineer for HS Doirani, including electrical systems officer, auxiliary machinery officer, materials inventory officer, damage control officer, and electronic systems officer. Ensured up to date maintenance on mechanical, electrical and electronic platform equipment including repairs and reoperations. Updated equipment manual library and authored ship\\\\u2019s entire register. Resumed of ship\\\\u2019s PMS system while maintaining 100% transparency in works\\\\/materials procurement.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2004-02-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2011-08-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Engineering Qualified Instructor and Fleet Headquarters\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Directed pre-vetting \\\\/ vetting, training, and evaluations of various types of HN vessels, overseeing routine engineering, mechanical engineering, emergency actions, damage control, environmental safety, and staff. Compiled vetting \\\\/ evaluation reports and \\\\u2018lessons learned\\\\u2019 reports using MS Word. Presented lessons learned to staff using MS PowerPoint in order to increase awareness and improve knowledge. Assisted with vetting and training preparations while maintaining computer network.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"2000-09-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2004-02-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Technical Supervisor, Aft Engineroom, HS Salamis\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Operation, maintainance and repairs, MTU main diesel engines, RENK TACKE reduction gears, ROCHEM reverse osmosis desalination systems, WESFALIA centrifugal separators, air compressors and other auxiliary machinery. Junior personnel consulting and training\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"1998-08-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"2000-08-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"The Greek Embassy, Washington, DC\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"The Greek Embassy, Washington, DC\\",\\"company_id\\":null,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":null,\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Procurement Officer, Hellenic Naval Attache\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Diplomat, offering HR services for Hellenic Navy\\\\u2019s student and personnel in the U.S., public and U.S. Government relations, assistant to the technical and procurement divisions, technical advisor to the Naval Attach\\\\u00e9.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"1996-10-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"1998-08-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/www.linkedin.com\\\\/company\\\\/hellenic-navy\\",\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Technical Supervisor, Fwd Engineroom, HS SPETSAI\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Technical supervisor, FW engine compartment, which included two (2) main gas turbines GE LM2500, two (2) SAUER & SOHN air compressors, one (1) WESTFALIA SEPARATORS fuel oil centrifugal separator and other auxiliary systems.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"1995-08-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"1996-10-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy, Skaramanga Shipyards Navy Echelon\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy, Skaramanga Shipyards Navy Echelon\\",\\"company_id\\":null,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":null,\\"department\\":\\"\\",\\"title\\":\\"Construction Monitoring and Technical Support\\",\\"highest_level\\":\\"individual contributor\\",\\"description\\":\\"Monitoring the construction of HS Spetsai and providing technical support, as a future on board engnieroom tech. supervisor. At the same time, he provided technical support to the under construction platforms of HS Psara and HS Salamis.\\",\\"last_updated\\":\\"2024-08-20T07:41:35.592379\\",\\"sub_department\\":\\"\\",\\"is_current\\":false},{\\"start_date\\":\\"1992-10-01\\",\\"end_date\\":\\"1995-08-01\\",\\"company\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_name\\":\\"Hellenic Navy\\",\\"company_id\\":8918703,\\"company_linkedin_url\\":