et of $11M. Responsible for FINANCIAL, TECHNICAL, OPERATIONAL and HSSE assurances across the vessels contributing to the fleet’s overall performance targeting no harm, no pollution, no incident achieving GOAL ZERO. •Having worked at both Management and Operational levels, always been able to achieve goals with utmost efficiency and proficiency as reflected in my all-round performance. •Possess knowledge and experience of managing daily running of the vessel, planning long term maintenance, asset/ manpower mobilisation, budget development and management, adhering to the same and ensuring vessels deliver their targets safely, reliably, cost effectively using all resources wisely. •An excellent team player achieving goals with utmost efficiency and proficiency. •Engaged and participated to instigate various concepts improving digitalisation, data collection, hse collaboration and knowledge sharing hence improving the overall safety cultural and business ratings. •Actively involved in developing and improving the safety culture on board during all operational conditions, developing and ensuring compliance and good records to maintain vessels reliability, operability and commercial acceptance.", "company_name": "Wah Kwong Maritime Transport Holdings Limited", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "senior", "sub_department": "Systems", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/wah-kwong-maritime-transport-holdings-limited"}, {"title": "Senior Marine Engineer", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2022-06-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "Customer_service", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2016-06-01", "description": "•Appointed as part of the SMT( Senior Management Team) on Q flex and Qmax Vessels maintaining operational and commercial readiness at all times. As a senior member of the shipboard management team, I have had the opportunity to manage the vessel’s daily running including planning daily operations, long term maintenance, budgeting of the vessel at hand. Always actively involved in developing and improving the safety culture on board during all operational conditions. Having given inputs to reduce administrative workload during my office term. •I also had the opportunity to get a first-hand insight into the construction of a gas cargo tank during the repairs of one of our QFlex vessel after a collision into her cargo and ballast tank. (NO 96 construction). I was the sole 2nd engineer cargo responsible for taking the vessel into dock after the collision and then taking her out of dock and bringing her back into full sea service after completion of her 6-month long repairs in dock.", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "senior", "sub_department": "Support", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/shell"}, {"title": "Gas eng", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2016-06-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2016-05-01", "description": "", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/shell"}, {"title": "Assistant Engineer Superintendent", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2016-05-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "Engineering", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2015-06-01", "description": "•Key technical responsibility for the management of Al Kharaitiyat, Lijmiliya , Al Mayeda, Onaiza with annual budget of $27M. Responsible for HSSE across the vessels and achieved Zero TRC for fleet with over 3.5 million vessels managing an man hours. •Successfully implemented ‘Step Change in Leadership programme’ for fleet personnel to empower personnel to make decisions and take responsibility which led to overall improved performance. •An excellent team player having worked at both Management and Operational levels, having always been able to achieve goals with utmost efficiency and proficiency as reflected in my all-round performance. •Possess knowledge and experience of managing daily running of the vessel, planning long term maintenance and asset/ manpower mobilisation, budget development on yearly basis, managing budgets and adhering to the same and ensuring vessels deliver their said targets safely, reliably, cost effectively using all the resources at disposal wisely. •Was part of the disaster management, emergency response and relief team for one of our vessels which had an incident in the Suez Canal during having first-hand experience and knowledge on the same.", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/shell"}, {"title": "3rd Engineer", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2015-06-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "Engineering", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2011-09-01", "description": "", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "None", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/shell"}, {"title": "4th Engineer", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2011-09-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "Engineering", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2009-04-01", "description": "", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "", "company_linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/shell"}, {"title": "Graduate Engineering Trainee", "company": "Shell", "end_date": "2009-04-01", "company_id": 1271, "department": "Sales", "is_current": false, "start_date": "2007-09-01", "description": "", "company_name": "Shell", "last_updated": "2024-09-28T02:08:58.313931", "highest_level": "individual contributor", "sub_department": "Accounts", "company_linkedin